  "notes": "Cash-basis village with governmental (General, Street, Fire) and proprietary (Water, Sewer, Electric) funds. Governmental lines from the Total column of the governmental receipts/disbursements statement (p4). Governmental interest income 7,229 and business-type interest/capital outlay/debt service are printed below the totals under 'Other financing sources' / 'Other receipts (disbursements)' and recorded as outside_printed_total items. Governmental beginning 255,233 (fund balance as cash), restated by +19,183 prior period adjustment (p4). Business-type roll-forward: 368,072 + 346,094 + 7,130 - 168,569 - 40,351 - 36,040 - 51,413 - 14,430 = 410,493 (printed total disbursements 168,570 is 1 high). Business-type transfers net -14,430 (in 74,768, out 89,198). Balance sheet is the government-wide cash-basis Statement of Net Position, Total column; Due From/Due To 68,488 are internal balances. Detail: the budgetary all-funds schedule (p11) mixes governmental and business-type funds in its receipts lines and the comparative statements (pp9-10) repeat the basic statements, so detail is left empty to avoid double counting. Governmental ending balance 257,246 is the fund balance the p4 statement rolls forward; the Statement of Assets and Fund Balances (p3) shows it as cash 185,343 + cash with County Treasurer 3,414 (= 188,757 actual cash) + Due From 68,488 (interfund receivable), with Due To 17,122 shown as a liability (total fund balances 240,123; 'Total cash basis fund balances' 257,246 = total assets), so the rolled-forward balance includes interfund balances. Read pages 1-11 of 11. Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p4, p6) replace the combined schedule.",
  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "Should the Budgetary Basis Budget and Actual - All Funds schedule (p11) be recorded in detail? Its disbursement lines are by fund (General 338,068 and Street 34,561 governmental; Water 74,287, Sewer 120,654, Electric 101,432 business-type) but its receipt lines (Taxes, Charges for services 372,171, Grants/donations/misc 106,894, Other 14,024, Transfers in 108,005) mix governmental and business-type funds and do not split cleanly from the p4/p6 statements, so detail is currently empty.",
      "amount": 802257,
      "recorded_as": "detail [] (schedule not recorded)",
      "source_page": 11
    }
  ]
